    differences:
      "The Book of Gates' hall is part of the sun god's night journey, painted for kings, and its labels are in a cryptic script; the Book of the Dead scene is the judgment of one named private person, Ani, and its speeches are about his own heart.",
    wordingComparable: "no",
    meaningComparable: "partly",
    transmissionEvidence:
      "None shown. Both draw on the same New Kingdom ideas of judgment before Osiris; nothing shows that one scene was modelled on the other. Proposed only as a conceptual parallel, never as transmission.",
